{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41718172",
      "title": "Storing Server Actions in Separate Files",
      "sourceHash": "fe8f7c64dc3349fda018d9680a27c2e58376832792e2a4045f3a1ebf29a440ed",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.45,
          "end": 3.24,
          "en": "So this is how we can add a Server action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.24,
          "end": 6.96,
          "en": "There also is another way of adding it though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.96,
          "end": 9.48,
          "en": "You can add it in a component like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.48,
          "end": 11.545,
          "en": "but this will only work if the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.545,
          "end": 15.84,
          "en": "in which you are adding it is not a client component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.84,
          "end": 18.262,
          "en": "If you had use client here at the top",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.262,
          "end": 21.103,
          "en": "because somewhere else in the component you might be using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.103,
          "end": 24.918,
          "en": "some client-only feature, you would get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.918,
          "end": 28.35,
          "en": "that you are not allowed to have server actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.35,
          "end": 30.603,
          "en": "in a client component file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.648,
          "end": 34.29,
          "en": "So that would be a problem then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.29,
          "end": 36.96,
          "en": "Of course, here we don't need use client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.96,
          "end": 39.45,
          "en": "though actually later we will need it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.45,
          "end": 41.924,
          "en": "but at the moment we would be fine like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.924,
          "end": 45.51,
          "en": "but nonetheless this would be a potential problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.51,
          "end": 47.61,
          "en": "In addition, you also might not want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.61,
          "end": 49.89,
          "en": "to have your server-side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.89,
          "end": 53.04,
          "en": "form submission handling logic in the same file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.04,
          "end": 54.57,
          "en": "as your JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.57,
          "end": 57.39,
          "en": "You might want to separate that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.39,
          "end": 58.92,
          "en": "And for those reasons,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.92,
          "end": 62.313,
          "en": "you can also store server actions in separate files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.455,
          "end": 65.61,
          "en": "Therefore, here, I'll actually go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.61,
          "end": 67.83,
          "en": "to that root lip folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 67.83,
          "end": 70.65,
          "en": "and add a actions.js file in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 70.65,
          "end": 73.44,
          "en": "though the file name does not matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 73.44,
          "end": 76.86,
          "en": "It doesn't have to be named actions.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 76.86,
          "end": 78.003,
          "en": "it could be any name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 78.936,
          "end": 81.66,
          "en": "What's important in that file though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 81.66,
          "end": 85.513,
          "en": "is that it has that Use Server directive at the top.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 85.513,
          "end": 88.23,
          "en": "So now not inside of a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 88.23,
          "end": 90.981,
          "en": "but instead at the top of a file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 90.981,
          "end": 93.27000000000001,
          "en": "When adding it at the top",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 93.27000000000001,
          "end": 97.17,
          "en": "of a file like this, all the functions you might define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 97.17,
          "end": 101.27799999999999,
          "en": "in that file will be treated as Server Actions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 101.27799999999999,
          "end": 106.27799999999999,
          "en": "So that simply now allows us to go back to that Share page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.55799999999999,
          "end": 110.281,
          "en": "and grab that share meal function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 110.281,
          "end": 112.233,
          "en": "and cut it from there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.128,
          "end": 116.944,
          "en": "and instead move it into this Actions file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 116.944,
          "end": 119.36099999999999,
          "en": "There it now must be exported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 119.36099999999999,
          "end": 123.336,
          "en": "so that it can be used in other files, and you can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.336,
          "end": 126.3,
          "en": "and should now remove use server in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.3,
          "end": 128.973,
          "en": "because we already got that at the top of the file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 131.67,
          "end": 134.34,
          "en": "And with that server action outsourced here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.34,
          "end": 138.512,
          "en": "we can now go back to the share meal page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.512,
          "end": 142.62,
          "en": "and still use it as an action here on the forum",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.62,
          "end": 144.423,
          "en": "by simply importing it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.19,
          "end": 148.233,
          "en": "So by adding this import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 149.91,
          "end": 152.97,
          "en": "And now you would be able to convert this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.97,
          "end": 155.19299999999998,
          "en": "to a client component if you needed to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 156.06,
          "end": 159.75,
          "en": "Now, you would not get an error when doing that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 159.75,
          "end": 162.69,
          "en": "and that might sound strange, but the problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 162.69,
          "end": 166.2,
          "en": "before was simply that you were defining client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 166.2,
          "end": 169.53,
          "en": "and server-side code in the same file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 169.53,
          "end": 171.48,
          "en": "and the build process that's used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 171.48,
          "end": 174.93,
          "en": "by NextJS is essentially not able to separate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 174.93,
          "end": 178.77,
          "en": "that in a clean way, and therefore server-side code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 178.77,
          "end": 181.65,
          "en": "could accidentally end up on the client side,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 181.65,
          "end": 184.05,
          "en": "which could pose security issues",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 184.05,
          "end": 186.183,
          "en": "and cause other problems as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 187.05,
          "end": 189.12,
          "en": "That's why for technical reasons,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 189.12,
          "end": 191.22,
          "en": "you can't mix both in the same file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 191.22,
          "end": 194.19,
          "en": "but you can absolutely import a server action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 194.19,
          "end": 196.32,
          "en": "from another file and then use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 196.32,
          "end": 198.736,
          "en": "in such a client component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 198.736,
          "end": 201.51,
          "en": "Again, here we don't need use client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 201.51,
          "end": 203.31,
          "en": "but it is important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 203.31,
          "end": 205.65,
          "en": "that you can blend these two worlds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 205.65,
          "end": 209.103,
          "en": "and mix these two worlds, as I just described it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 210.192,
          "end": 213.81,
          "en": "But with that, it's now finally time to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 213.81,
          "end": 216.9,
          "en": "that we're not just logging the meal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 216.9,
          "end": 220.2,
          "en": "but that we're actually storing it in a database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 220.2,
          "end": 223.263,
          "en": "and that we store the image on the file system.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}